1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,586
Guys, guys, I've
got great news.

2
00:00:02,628 --> 00:00:03,712
Guess what.

3
00:00:03,754 --> 00:00:05,339
Uh... Monica's pregnant.

4
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,256
Really?

5
00:00:08,091 --> 00:00:10,803
Let's get past the moment.

6
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:11,887
What-what's your news?

7
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:12,888
Thank you.

8
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:15,223
I got a job in advertising.

9
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:16,266
Hey!

10
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:18,519
Honey, that's incredible!

11
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,562
Gosh, what's
the pay like?

12
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,900
Oh, come on, people.

13
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:26,360
Come on now.

14
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,028
If I don't know
who makes the most,

15
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:29,655
how do I know who
I like the most?

16
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:30,656
Hi, Joey.

17
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,160
Well, actually it pays nothing.
It's an internship.

18
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:37,245
Oh, that's cool. We have interns
at Days of Our Lives.

19
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:40,499
Right, so it'll be the same,
except less sex with you.

20
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:42,292
ROSS:
So, uh, what
kind of stuff

21
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:44,628
do you think
they'll have you do there?

22
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:46,045
Well, it's a training program,

23
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,965
but at the end,
they hire the people they like.

24
00:00:48,007 --> 00:00:49,717
That's great.

25
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:52,093
Yeah, I mean, there's probably
going to be some gruntwork,

26
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,595
which will probably stink.

27
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:54,930
You know, a grown man
getting people coffee

28
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:57,641
is a little humiliating.

29
00:00:57,683 --> 00:01:00,143
Humiliating and noble.

30
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,270
Thank you.

31
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,441
You know, if-if I didn't
already have a job,

32
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,361
I think I would have been
really good in advertising.

33
00:01:09,403 --> 00:01:12,322
Ross, you did not come up
with "Got Milk?"

34
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:14,449
Yes, I did! I did!

35
00:01:15,659 --> 00:01:18,161
I should have written it down.

36
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:30,424
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

37
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,801
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

38
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:35,303
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

39
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:40,183
♪ It's like you're always stuck
in second gear ♪

40
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:43,186
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

41
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:44,772
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

42
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:48,859
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

43
00:01:48,901 --> 00:01:51,278
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

44
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:53,739
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

45
00:01:53,781 --> 00:01:55,032
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

46
00:01:55,074 --> 00:01:58,786
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

47
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:02,664
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

48
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:09,421
( knocking )

49
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:10,297
Hey.
Hey.

50
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:11,465
Where's Chandler?

51
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:12,800
I want to wish him good luck

52
00:02:12,841 --> 00:02:13,801
on his first day.

53
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:16,386
And I smelled bacon. Ha-ha.

54
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:18,097
He just left.

55
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,807
Who did?

56
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:23,102
Joey, you're never going
to believe it.

57
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,103
She called.

58
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:25,437
She did?
You got it!

59
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:26,605
I did?!

60
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:27,898
What is she talking about?

61
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,775
I don't know, but
it sounds great!

62
00:02:29,817 --> 00:02:31,150
No, your agent called.

63
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:32,527
You got that audition!

64
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,654
With Leonard Hayes?
Yes!

65
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:34,655
Oh, my God,
that is great!

66
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:35,656
That is great.

67
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:37,449
It's for a play on Broadway.

68
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:38,826
And in a real theater.

69
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,077
Not that little one

70
00:02:40,119 --> 00:02:42,203
underneath the deli
like last time.

71
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,538
Is it a good play?

72
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:44,790
Well, it must be,
because I read it,

73
00:02:44,832 --> 00:02:46,458
and I didn't understand
a single word!

74
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:49,503
And Leonard Hayes
is starring in it.

75
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:50,963
Yeah, yeah,
and directing.

76
00:02:51,005 --> 00:02:53,381
Oh, he was so good in that movie
of Macbeth.

77
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:54,508
You saw that?

78
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:57,260
No, but I saw the previews.

79
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:58,929
They played it
right before Jackass.

80
00:02:58,971 --> 00:03:01,180
Oh.
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

81
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,266
He has. Yeah, he's
done some amazing work.

82
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:06,103
Oh, yeah. Oh, I loved him
in those cell phone commercials.

83
00:03:06,145 --> 00:03:07,771
I know. When the
monkey hits him

84
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:09,731
in the face with
giant rubber phone.

85
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:11,817
Hey, maybe the monkey will be
at the audition.

86
00:03:11,859 --> 00:03:14,319
Don't make me more nervous
than I already am.

87
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:25,831
Good morning, everybody.

88
00:03:25,873 --> 00:03:27,248
Can I get you a
cup of coffee, sir?

89
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,458
Oh, no, no, no.

90
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,460
I'm an intern,
just like you guys,

91
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:33,254
except for the tie,
the briefcase, and...

92
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,382
the fact that I can rent a car.

93
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:37,425
Seriously,
you're an intern?

94
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,011
Yeah, well, I'm kind of heading

95
00:03:39,053 --> 00:03:41,096
in a new career direction,
and, you know,

96
00:03:41,138 --> 00:03:42,430
you got to start
at the bottom.

97
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:44,349
Dude.

98
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:45,767
All right, look, I know

99
00:03:45,809 --> 00:03:48,020
I'm a little bit older
than you guys,

100
00:03:48,062 --> 00:03:50,022
but it's not like I'm Bob Hope.

101
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:53,775
The comedian?

102
00:03:53,817 --> 00:03:55,027
USO?

103
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,572
Uh, it's USA, sir.

104
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:07,414
This is Joey Tribbiani.

105
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:08,707
Joey, these are the producers,

106
00:04:08,749 --> 00:04:10,167
and as you probably
already know,

107
00:04:10,209 --> 00:04:11,168
this is Leonard Hayes.

108
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:12,211
Hi.

109
00:04:12,251 --> 00:04:16,173
Wow.

110
00:04:16,215 --> 00:04:18,133
It is so amazing to meet you.

111
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:20,343
I am such a big fan
of your work.

112
00:04:20,385 --> 00:04:21,762
Well, I've, uh,

113
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:23,346
I've been blessed
with, uh, a lot of...

114
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,431
a lot of great roles.

115
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:26,892
Oh, tell me about it, huh.

116
00:04:26,934 --> 00:04:29,770
Unlimited nights and weekends.

117
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:32,064
Are you making fun of me?

118
00:04:32,106 --> 00:04:34,233
Because I am
not a sellout.

119
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:36,317
I didn't do that for the money.

120
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:38,028
I believe in those phones.

121
00:04:38,070 --> 00:04:41,656
I almost lost a cousin
because of bad wireless service.

122
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:43,700
No, no. I-I wasn't making fun
of you, honestly.

123
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:45,702
I-I think you were great
in those commercials.

124
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:47,037
Really?
Yeah.

125
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:48,455
Well, I do

126
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:50,749
bring a certain credibility
to the role.

127
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:51,959
It's true.

128
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,252
Are you kidding?

129
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:55,129
When they shoot you
out of that cannon...

130
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:57,380
Hang up that phone.

131
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:58,882
One take.

132
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:00,092
Wow.

133
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:01,927
We did that
in one take.

134
00:05:01,969 --> 00:05:03,762
So, shall we, uh, read?

135
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:04,972
Oh, yeah, sure.

136
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,181
Top of act two.

137
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:07,224
This is my entrance.

138
00:05:07,266 --> 00:05:08,267
You got it?

139
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,350
Mm-hmm.

140
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:14,522
What the hell are
you still doing here?

141
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:16,357
Ooh!

142
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,818
Uh...

143
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,318
I think you know.

144
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,487
Bastard!

145
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,822
I am what you made me.

146
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:22,823
You know what?

147
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,199
I could go right now.

148
00:05:24,241 --> 00:05:25,450
Go, go.

149
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:26,868
I can't.

150
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:29,163
Oh, I want to, Long Pause.

151
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:35,252
But I can't.

152
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:37,087
I'm so sorry.

153
00:05:37,129 --> 00:05:40,548
You-you... you're not
supposed to say "Long Pause."

154
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:45,053
Oh.

155
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:47,014
Oh, I thought
that was your character's name.

156
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,473
You know?

157
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:50,100
I thought you were, like,
an Indian or something.

158
00:05:50,142 --> 00:05:51,726
You know with the...

159
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:52,727
Sorry.

160
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,437
Long Pause. No.

161
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:56,439
Thank you so much
for coming in.

162
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:57,691
We appreciate it.
Thank you.

163
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:58,900
Well, are you sure

164
00:05:58,942 --> 00:06:00,068
you don't want me
to do it again?

165
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,486
I could do it...
with an accent?

166
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:03,197
You know, Southern.

167
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:05,866
( Jamaican accent ):
I could go right now, mon.

168
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,909
Huh?

169
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:11,746
My God in heaven.

170
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,540
Joey, hang on for a second.

171
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:16,210
Leonard, can we talk
to you for a moment?

172
00:06:16,251 --> 00:06:17,544
Yes.

173
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:18,962
Listen, I'm going
to bring him back.

174
00:06:19,004 --> 00:06:20,339
You... you've got
to be kidding.

175
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:21,548
He-he can't act.

176
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:23,550
I can work
with him and...

177
00:06:23,591 --> 00:06:25,260
Hey, I-I don't care
if you think he's hot.

178
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:26,887
You know, if you want
to sleep with him,

179
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:27,888
do it on your own time.

180
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,097
This is a play.

181
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:30,307
Leonard, I'm
bringing him back.

182
00:06:30,349 --> 00:06:31,599
No, listen.

183
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:34,061
If you insist on this,
I will call my agent

184
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:35,312
so fast on a cell phone

185
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:37,189
that has a connection
that is so clear,

186
00:06:37,231 --> 00:06:38,940
he's going to think
I'm next door.

187
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:41,651
Uh, hi. Uh...

188
00:06:41,693 --> 00:06:43,904
thank you so much
for whispering for my benefit,

189
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,404
but, um, look.

190
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:47,032
If you just tell me
what I did wrong,

191
00:06:47,074 --> 00:06:48,825
I would love to work on it
and come back

192
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:49,993
and try it again for you.

193
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:52,371
And-and, also, how you doin'?

194
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:54,497
( laughs )

195
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:57,084
If you please, just-just
give me another chance.

196
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,585
I really want to get better.

197
00:06:58,626 --> 00:06:59,961
Please.

198
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:01,671
Well... well,

199
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:03,924
if you want to come back
at the end of the day today,

200
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,008
here are my
notes. Ready?

201
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,009
Yeah, yeah.

202
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:07,344
Um, you're in your head.

203
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:09,096
You're-you're thinking
way too much.

204
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:10,389
I really doubt that.

205
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:11,848
No, no, no, no, no.

206
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:14,268
It's that... it's that
you're not connected

207
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:15,977
with anything
in your body.

208
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:17,145
There's no urgency.

209
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:18,521
The scene
is a struggle.
Uh-huh.

210
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:19,814
It's a...
it's a race.
Uh-huh.

211
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,942
Also, what you did
was horizontal.

212
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,860
Don't be afraid
to explore...

213
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:25,195
the vertical,
you know?

214
00:07:25,237 --> 00:07:27,364
Uh-huh.
And don't learn
the words.

215
00:07:27,406 --> 00:07:29,448
Let the words learn you.

216
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:37,498
Couldn't I just sleep
with the producer?

217
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:43,380
Hey, do you want
to go to dinner tonight?

218
00:07:43,422 --> 00:07:45,048
Oh, I can't.

219
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:47,426
I've-I've got a date with
that waitress, uh, Katie.

220
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,718
Yeah. I-I know

221
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:49,886
we've only gone
out, like, twice,

222
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:51,096
but I don't know.

223
00:07:51,138 --> 00:07:52,722
I have a really good
feeling about her.

224
00:07:52,764 --> 00:07:54,182
Oh, I hear divorce bells.

225
00:07:54,224 --> 00:07:55,642
Uh.

226
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,394
All right, just
give me your wallets,

227
00:07:57,436 --> 00:07:58,770
and there won't be a problem.

228
00:07:58,812 --> 00:07:59,896
What?

229
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:01,106
I have a gun.

230
00:08:01,148 --> 00:08:02,232
Okay, just-just
relax, Phoebe.

231
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:04,401
Just stay calm.

232
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,071
Oh, my God, I can't
find my wallet!

233
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:12,742
All right, lady,
now give me your purse.

234
00:08:12,784 --> 00:08:14,286
No.

235
00:08:14,328 --> 00:08:15,745
What do you mean, no?

236
00:08:15,787 --> 00:08:18,415
I knew you'd be my
death, Phoebe Buffay!

237
00:08:18,457 --> 00:08:20,541
Lowell, is that you?

238
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:22,294
Phoebe?

239
00:08:22,336 --> 00:08:23,628
Oh, my God!
Unbelievable.

240
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:24,796
Oh, my God.

241
00:08:24,838 --> 00:08:27,757
Oh. Well, I'm sorry,
I'm sorry.

242
00:08:27,799 --> 00:08:30,093
Ross, this is my old friend
Lowell from the streets.

243
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:31,678
( laughs )

244
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:32,846
Lowell, Ross.

245
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,389
Ross, nice to meet you.

246
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:36,724
Yeah, a real pleasure.

247
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:39,394
Oh. It's been so long.

248
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:41,104
Oh, so long.

249
00:08:41,146 --> 00:08:42,939
I can't believe you're
still doing this.

250
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:44,774
Uh, I know...
but I quit smoking.

251
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:45,733
Good for you.

252
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,152
So, you look

253
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:48,611
like you're doing
really well.

254
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:50,197
I guess your mugging days
are behind you.

255
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:51,448
Oh.

256
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:53,033
Oh, my God!

257
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,993
Phoebe, you used to mug people?

258
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:57,162
Excuse me, Ross.

259
00:08:57,204 --> 00:08:59,414
Old friends
catching up.

260
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,000
( laughing )

261
00:09:03,126 --> 00:09:04,669
Hey.

262
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:06,087
Hey. How did the audition go?

263
00:09:06,129 --> 00:09:08,256
Well, they want
to see me again this afternoon,

264
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:10,300
but, uh, boy, Leonard Hayes
did not like me.

265
00:09:10,342 --> 00:09:12,302
What happened?

266
00:09:12,344 --> 00:09:14,804
Uh, he said I wasn't urgent
enough, you know,

267
00:09:14,846 --> 00:09:17,140
and that everything I did
was horizontal,

268
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:21,102
and I should be more vertical.

269
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:23,646
Oh, and he said
that I should think less.

270
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:24,981
Well, so far, so good.

271
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,194
Honey, I'm old.

272
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:31,530
What's wrong?

273
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,740
I am so much older
than other these interns.

274
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:35,325
I can't compete with them.

275
00:09:35,367 --> 00:09:37,118
So, you're a
little older.

276
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,246
Try to look at
the positive.

277
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:41,789
You have all this
life experience.

278
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:42,999
Yes, but I don't think

279
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:45,001
life experience
is going to help me...

280
00:09:45,043 --> 00:09:47,504
with these.

281
00:09:47,546 --> 00:09:50,507
Wow!

282
00:09:50,549 --> 00:09:52,800
It's like they're on fire.

283
00:09:58,098 --> 00:09:59,516
What are they?

284
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:00,850
They're these
prototype sneakers,

285
00:10:00,892 --> 00:10:02,227
and I have to come up with ideas

286
00:10:02,269 --> 00:10:03,770
on how to sell them,
which I can't do,

287
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:06,022
because no self-respecting adult
would ever wear these.

288
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,732
I'll give you $500 for them.

289
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:13,405
What am I supposed
to do with these?

290
00:10:13,447 --> 00:10:14,948
All right, come on.
Sneakers are easy.

291
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:16,324
You wear sneakers all the time.

292
00:10:16,366 --> 00:10:17,658
Well, first of all,

293
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,536
they're not called sneakers
anymore.

294
00:10:19,578 --> 00:10:22,163
Apparently, they're called
"kicks" or "skids."

295
00:10:22,205 --> 00:10:24,916
And I think heard somebody say
"slorps."

296
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:27,919
Here, look.

297
00:10:27,961 --> 00:10:30,004
They got these wheels
that pop out from the bottom

298
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:31,631
so you can roll around,

299
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:33,800
because, apparently,
walking is too much exercise.

300
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:37,471
Kids, kids, roll your way
to childhood obesity.

301
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:42,476
Would you help me
try to sell these?

302
00:10:42,517 --> 00:10:47,688
Okay, have you considered
using a girl with huge knockers?

303
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:50,317
I-I don't think that's the kind
of thing they're looking for.

304
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:52,819
Hey, that'd work on me.

305
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:55,196
Why do you think
I buy Mrs. Butterworth's?

306
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:05,165
Hey.

307
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:06,583
Hey.
Hey.

308
00:11:06,625 --> 00:11:08,126
Hey, you'll never guess
what just happened.

309
00:11:08,168 --> 00:11:09,628
( groans )
Phoebe and I
got mugged!

310
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:11,129
Are you okay?

311
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:13,923
Yeah, because Phoebe
knew the mugger.

312
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:16,134
How do you know a mugger?

313
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:19,304
I'm sorry I have friends
outside the six of us.

314
00:11:19,346 --> 00:11:21,556
You want to know
how she knew him?

315
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:23,933
Because Phoebe
used to mug people.

316
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:25,352
Seriously?

317
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:27,562
Well, I'm not proud of it.

318
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:31,732
But, you know, sometimes,
when I was living on the street

319
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:34,986
and I needed money for food
and stuff, I...

320
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:36,363
Phoebe, that is awful.

321
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:39,157
Well, okay, I wasn't rich
like you guys, okay?

322
00:11:39,199 --> 00:11:43,286
I didn't eat gold
and have a flying pony.

323
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:44,787
I had a hard life.

324
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:47,624
My mother was killed
by a drug dealer.

325
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:49,000
Your mother killed herself.

326
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,960
She was a drug dealer!

327
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:55,714
Well, anyway, it was
a good thing Phoebe knew him

328
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:58,343
because I was about to do
some serious damage.

329
00:11:58,385 --> 00:11:59,886
( chuckling ):
Okay.

330
00:12:01,221 --> 00:12:02,721
Wow, this must have brought back

331
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,599
some really bad memories
for you, Ross.

332
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:06,184
Why?

333
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:07,644
Well, Ross was mugged as a kid.

334
00:12:07,686 --> 00:12:09,187
You were?
Yeah.

335
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:10,647
And it was pretty traumatic.

336
00:12:10,689 --> 00:12:12,357
It was outside
St. Mark's Comics.

337
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:15,026
You know, I was just there
minding my own business,

338
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,944
you know, seeing what kind
of trouble

339
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,530
Spider-Man got into that week.

340
00:12:18,572 --> 00:12:20,781
( coughing ):
Wonder Woman.

341
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:24,202
Anyway, I was heading towards
this bakery, you know,

342
00:12:24,244 --> 00:12:27,746
to pick up a couple of dozen
Linzertortes for someone.

343
00:12:30,584 --> 00:12:33,670
When out of nowhere, this-this
thug with a pipe jumps out

344
00:12:33,712 --> 00:12:35,672
and says,
"Give me your money, punk!"

345
00:12:35,714 --> 00:12:37,298
Oh, my God.
I know.

346
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:39,634
Yeah, and the worst part was
they took my backpack

347
00:12:39,676 --> 00:12:41,802
which had all the original
artwork I had done

348
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:45,764
for my own comic book,
Science Boy.

349
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:46,974
Oh, yeah.

350
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,143
What was his superpower again?

351
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:52,188
A superhuman thirst
for knowledge.

352
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:55,567
I-I better get to class.

353
00:12:55,609 --> 00:12:57,318
Are there any more
of your friends

354
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,320
I should look out for
on my way, Phoebe?

355
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:02,574
No. Actually, you might want
to stay away from Jane Street.

356
00:13:02,616 --> 00:13:04,284
That's where Stabby Joe works.

357
00:13:08,787 --> 00:13:10,749
Okay, I think we
have a problem here.

358
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:12,250
What?

359
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:14,793
Well, um, back in my
mugging days, you know,

360
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:16,755
I, um, I worked
St. Mark's Comics.

361
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:18,465
Yeah?

362
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:21,551
Well, a pipe was
my weapon of choice.

363
00:13:21,593 --> 00:13:25,597
And, um, preteen comic
book nerds were my meat.

364
00:13:26,681 --> 00:13:28,475
So?

365
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:29,976
Well, there was
this one kid

366
00:13:30,017 --> 00:13:32,103
who had a sticker on
his backpack that said,

367
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:34,564
"Geology rocks."
"Geology rocks."

368
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:38,777
Oh, my God.

369
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,570
I know! I mugged Ross!

370
00:13:47,494 --> 00:13:48,453
You're late.

371
00:13:48,495 --> 00:13:49,579
I know, I'm sorry.

372
00:13:49,621 --> 00:13:50,829
But can I just have
a quick second

373
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:51,914
to run to the bathroom?

374
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,792
No. Leonard doesn't wait.

375
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:56,210
But I am bursting with Yoo-hoo.

376
00:13:57,295 --> 00:13:58,421
Joey, here we go.

377
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:00,047
Let's go, very quickly.

378
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,257
Actually, I really need...

379
00:14:01,299 --> 00:14:02,592
We must go now, quickly, please.

380
00:14:02,634 --> 00:14:03,718
Okay, yes, sir.

381
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:04,719
Aah...

382
00:14:04,761 --> 00:14:06,137
Ready?

383
00:14:06,179 --> 00:14:08,723
What the hell are you
still doing here?

384
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,642
I think you know.

385
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:13,060
Oh, you sick bastard.

386
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:14,646
I am what you made me.

387
00:14:14,688 --> 00:14:16,063
You know what?
What?

388
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:19,567
I could go right now.

389
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:21,611
Then go, go.

390
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:23,196
Oh, I-I can't.

391
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:27,367
I want to, but I can't.

392
00:14:28,451 --> 00:14:30,036
Cut.

393
00:14:30,077 --> 00:14:31,371
That was good.

394
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:32,706
That was very good.

395
00:14:32,747 --> 00:14:34,415
You did everything
I asked for.

396
00:14:34,457 --> 00:14:36,417
I did?
Yes, plus, what,
you've got this,

397
00:14:36,459 --> 00:14:38,127
I don't know
what you got going--

398
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:39,587
this squirmy quality

399
00:14:39,629 --> 00:14:40,963
Well, I...
that you're bringing
to the character

400
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,382
that I couldn't
have even imagined.

401
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,008
Wow. Hey, here's what
we're going to do.

402
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,885
Come back tomorrow
for the final call-backs

403
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,512
with the backers,
do all of this--

404
00:14:47,554 --> 00:14:49,806
what you got going now--
but you know what? More. More.

405
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:51,224
Can you do that?

406
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,726
Sure, yeah.
I-I don't have time

407
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,811
to say thank you
because I really got to go.

408
00:14:57,355 --> 00:14:58,481
Look at that.

409
00:14:58,523 --> 00:15:00,316
Still in character.

410
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:01,651
I like it.

411
00:15:01,693 --> 00:15:03,069
I plant seeds...

412
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:04,821
I can't explain it.

413
00:15:04,863 --> 00:15:06,531
I don't know.

414
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:11,327
Hey.

415
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:12,453
Hey.
What are you doing?

416
00:15:12,495 --> 00:15:13,788
Putting on
the sneakers.

417
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:15,248
Thought I'd get
in the younger mindset.

418
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:16,666
You know,
see if it sparked anything.

419
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:18,501
Oh, anything yet?

420
00:15:18,543 --> 00:15:19,960
Yes, how's this?

421
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:21,629
"They're so uncomfortable,

422
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:24,799
it's like getting kicked
in the nuts for your feet."

423
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:27,802
Hey.

424
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:29,011
Hi.
Hey.

425
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:34,308
( humming )
( rummaging )

426
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:39,980
Probably wondering
what I'm doing.

427
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:42,776
No, that seems about right.

428
00:15:42,817 --> 00:15:45,194
Yesterday, at my audition,
I really had to pee

429
00:15:45,236 --> 00:15:48,364
and apparently, having to pee
makes me a really good actor.

430
00:15:48,406 --> 00:15:50,867
I got a call-back,
so I'm drinking everything.

431
00:15:50,909 --> 00:15:52,326
Oh, hey, by the way.
Mm-hmm.

432
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:54,328
That eggnog in our fridge
was great.

433
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,414
Joey, that was formula.

434
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:59,041
We got to get more of that.

435
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:02,044
You know what,
these aren't half bad.

436
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:03,379
You should suggest

437
00:16:03,421 --> 00:16:05,339
something like these
to Ralph Lauren.

438
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,383
Okay, first of all,
that's stupid.

439
00:16:07,425 --> 00:16:10,678
And second of all, I'm not
allowed to talk to Ralph.

440
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,555
All right.

441
00:16:12,597 --> 00:16:14,181
I feel younger already.

442
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:20,772
Yeah, I think
I broke my hip.

443
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,149
Hey, you.

444
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,191
Hey.

445
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,359
Hey.

446
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,945
How was class?

447
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,529
No one ever asks me that.

448
00:16:28,571 --> 00:16:29,906
What's wrong?

449
00:16:29,948 --> 00:16:31,031
Nothing.

450
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:32,408
I really want to know.

451
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:34,076
Oh, uh...

452
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:36,871
Well, um, it was actually
a rather lively discussion

453
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:38,623
about the Pleistocene...

454
00:16:38,665 --> 00:16:41,334
All right,
nothing is worth this.

455
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,002
Um, I have a...
I have a confession to make.

456
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:47,214
Um, okay, you know that, um,
that girl that mugged you

457
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:48,466
when you were a kid?

458
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:49,968
What-what are you
talking about?

459
00:16:50,008 --> 00:16:51,302
It wasn't a girl.

460
00:16:51,344 --> 00:16:54,347
It was this-this huge dude.

461
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:55,640
You don't have
to lie anymore, Ross.

462
00:16:55,682 --> 00:16:58,058
I know that it was
a 14-year-old girl.

463
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,017
No, it wasn't.

464
00:16:59,059 --> 00:16:59,811
Yes, it was!

465
00:16:59,853 --> 00:17:01,228
No, it wasn't!

466
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,897
You don't think I would have
defended myself

467
00:17:02,939 --> 00:17:04,190
against a 14-year-old...

468
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:05,692
Give your money, punk.

469
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:08,110
Oh, my God, it was you!

470
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:09,988
I can't believe it.

471
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:13,533
You... you mugged me?!

472
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:14,701
Yeah.

473
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:16,202
And I'm so, so sorry, Ross.

474
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:17,954
I'm sorry.

475
00:17:17,996 --> 00:17:20,665
But, you know, if you think
about it, it's kind of neat.

476
00:17:20,707 --> 00:17:22,876
I mean,

477
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:24,210
well, it-it's just that

478
00:17:24,251 --> 00:17:26,212
I've always felt
kind of like an outsider.

479
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:27,630
You know, the rest of you

480
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:29,549
have these connections
that go way back.

481
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:35,013
And, you know, now you and I
have... have a great one.

482
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:38,016
It's not the best.

483
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:39,308
I know. I'm s...

484
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,560
Please, forgive me.

485
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:42,269
I don't know what to say.

486
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,062
There's nothing you can say.

487
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:46,232
That was the most humiliating
thing that ever happened to me.

488
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,650
Really?
Even more humiliating than...?

489
00:17:47,692 --> 00:17:49,610
Let's not do this.

490
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:54,741
...and then, at the
end of the commercial,

491
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:56,409
the girls get out
of the hot tub,

492
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,077
start making out
with each other.

493
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,119
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

494
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:03,457
That's interesting.

495
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:05,001
Just one thought.

496
00:18:05,043 --> 00:18:07,712
You didn't mention the shoes.

497
00:18:08,755 --> 00:18:11,424
Who's next?

498
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:13,133
Chandler.

499
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:15,636
Okay. You start on the image
of a guy putting on the shoes.

500
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:17,013
He's about my age.

501
00:18:17,055 --> 00:18:18,014
( scoffs ):
Your age?

502
00:18:18,056 --> 00:18:19,974
Uh-huh!

503
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,726
So, he's rolling
down the street

504
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:23,269
and he starts to lose control.

505
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:24,604
You know, maybe he falls.

506
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:26,146
Maybe he hurts himself.

507
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:29,442
Just then, a kid comes flying by
wearing the shoes.

508
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:32,110
He jumps over the old guy
and laughs.

509
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:36,950
And the line reads,
"Not suitable for adults."

510
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:39,077
Chandler, that's great.

511
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,120
Ah, thank you, sir.

512
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:44,540
Or
man-who's-two-years-younger-
than-me.

513
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:48,044
You see, that has
a clear selling point.

514
00:18:48,086 --> 00:18:50,129
It appeals to our
key demographic.

515
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,006
How did you come up with that?

516
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:53,758
I don't know, I don't know,
I don't know!

517
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:56,427
I was just... I tried
to get in the young mindset

518
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:58,638
and, you know,
stuff started to flow.

519
00:19:00,890 --> 00:19:02,767
Well, that is great.

520
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:04,018
Good work.

521
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,061
Thank you.

522
00:19:05,103 --> 00:19:06,938
We'll see all of you
tomorrow.

523
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:08,064
Okay.

524
00:19:16,447 --> 00:19:19,283
The cold weather hurts my hip.

525
00:19:24,122 --> 00:19:25,623
Hey, Ross.

526
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:27,458
Okay, look,

527
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,085
I know you're still
mad at me

528
00:19:29,127 --> 00:19:31,211
but can I just talk to you
for a sec?

529
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:32,212
Sure, go ahead.

530
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:33,213
Oh, sorry.

531
00:19:33,255 --> 00:19:35,091
Sure, go ahead.

532
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:39,012
I just really wanted
to apologize again.

533
00:19:39,053 --> 00:19:41,347
And-and also show you something

534
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:43,850
I think you'll find
very exciting.

535
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:47,227
Oh, my God!

536
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,729
"Crap from the street"!

537
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:57,905
Look, Ross, in this box are all
the things I got from mugging

538
00:19:57,947 --> 00:20:02,743
that I thought were too special
to sell... or smoke.

539
00:20:04,996 --> 00:20:08,206
Anyway, I was looking through it
and I found...

540
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:10,626
Science Boy.

541
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:14,922
( quietly ):
Oh, my God.

542
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,885
I never thought
I'd see this again.

543
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:21,054
What...? Uh...

544
00:20:21,095 --> 00:20:23,430
It's all here.

545
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:25,850
Oh, I-I...
Wha...?

546
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:28,144
What made you save it
all these years?

547
00:20:28,186 --> 00:20:30,396
I guess I just thought
it was really good.

548
00:20:30,437 --> 00:20:33,440
And-and maybe it would be worth
something one day.

549
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:37,778
You really thought Science Boy
was worth saving?

550
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,405
Well, yeah.

551
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:41,699
But you should know,
I also have a jar of Vaseline

552
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:43,034
and a cat skull in here.

553
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:48,246
Still, this-this is amazing.

554
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:49,415
Oh, my God.

555
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:50,917
Thank you, Phoebe.

556
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:52,251
Oh, you're welcome.

557
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:54,045
And thank you, for Science Boy.

558
00:20:54,087 --> 00:20:55,546
I learned a lot from him.

559
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:57,673
You're welcome.

560
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:01,761
I need an answer!

561
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:03,971
I-I can't tell you
something I don't know.

562
00:21:04,013 --> 00:21:05,056
You know!

563
00:21:05,098 --> 00:21:06,057
I don't know.

564
00:21:06,099 --> 00:21:08,434
I need an answer, now!

565
00:21:08,475 --> 00:21:09,518
All right, all right.

566
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:10,853
Here, you want an answer?

567
00:21:10,895 --> 00:21:12,188
The answer is...

568
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,652
Oh...!

569
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,571
She never loved me.

570
00:21:20,613 --> 00:21:22,448
She only loved you.

571
00:21:22,489 --> 00:21:24,283
You knew this all along
and you never told me?

572
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:25,952
You never told me?

573
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,536
I can never forgive you.
I can never forgive myself.

574
00:21:27,578 --> 00:21:29,329
I have nothing to live for.
Bang, end scene.

575
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,664
( breathing deeply )

576
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:34,877
Absolutely amazing.

577
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:38,338
The part is yours.

578
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,590
Oh, thanks.

579
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:41,175
Thanks. Now I really
have to get going...

580
00:21:41,217 --> 00:21:43,510
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait.

581
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:44,887
Congratulations.

582
00:21:44,929 --> 00:21:46,806
You did it. You did it.

583
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:48,599
Oh, you can relax now.

584
00:21:48,641 --> 00:21:49,642
Yeah.

585
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:52,019
( sighing with relief )

586
00:22:03,281 --> 00:22:05,616
Huh. You don't have a job,

587
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:09,578
but you have no problem
ordering porn.

588
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:12,414
On a Saturday afternoon?

589
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:15,918
I was in the house.

590
00:22:16,961 --> 00:22:20,714
Hey, uh, Phoebe didn't
by any chance mention that...?

591
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:23,383
She was the huge guy
that mugged you? Yeah.

592
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:25,094
I see.

593
00:22:25,136 --> 00:22:27,096
You didn't happen to tell...?

594
00:22:27,138 --> 00:22:28,973
Everybody we know? Yeah.

595
00:22:29,015 --> 00:22:31,017
Great. Thanks.

596
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:33,227
